          "description": "COLONY ENCRUSTINg, FORMINg bROAD, THICK UNILAMINAR SHEETS; OVERALL SIZE NOT KNOWN. AUTOZOOIDS bROADLY HEXAgONAL, SEPARATED bY FAINT gROOVES. FRONTAL SHIELD SMOOTHLY CALCIFIED, WITH 18 – 25 SMALL, ROUND FORAMINA, EACH ALMOST OCCLUDED bY A WELL-DEVELOPED OVAL LIgULA. PROXIMAL APERTURAL RIM RAISED, bEARINg ONE SMALL MEDIAN AVICULARIUM, PERPENDICULAR TO FRONTAL PLANE AND DISTALLY DIRECTED, AND A PAIR OF LATERAL AVICULARIA, ALSO PERPENDICULAR bUT WITH THE ROSTRUM FACINg DISTOLATERALLY INWARDS; SINgLE OR PAIRED AVICULARIA OCCASIONALLY PRESENT ON THE LATERAL RIM OF THE APERTURE, AND SPORADICALLY ON THE FRONTAL WALL. THE APERTURE IS ENCLOSED bY A THICKENED RIM, DEVELOPINg A SINgLE MEDIAN AVICULARIUM ON THE DISTAL EDgE. LARgE VICARIOUS AVICULARIA ARE PRESENT.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
